course: dictionary
lesson: 14877
title: Rebound: bouncing back
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and it can change its form. Rebound can be a verb (it rebounds, it rebounded) or a noun (a rebound). The words around it show which meaning fits. «The ball hit the wall and rebounded back to the player.» The ball bounced back after hitting the wall, so rebound means to bounce back after hitting something.
explain: Read this carefully: «Prices fell in June, but they rebounded in July.» Prices did not stay down. They went back up. So rebound can also mean to go back up after going down. Ask yourself: what is coming back, and from where?
explain: In basketball, a rebound is a noun. It is the ball you catch after a missed shot. «Maya jumped high and got the rebound.» Here rebound names the catch itself. In sport, you can also say the ball rebounds off the wall, the post or the backboard.
fact: Rebound means to bounce back after hitting something.
fact: In basketball, a rebound is catching the ball after a missed shot.
fact: «Prices rebounded» means prices went back up after they had gone down.
fact: Rebound can be a verb (rebounds, rebounded, rebounding) or a noun (a rebound).
fact: A bouncing ball rebounds because the surface it hits pushes back against it.
exercise: «The ball rebounded off the wall.» What does rebounded mean? | *To bounce back after hitting something | To break into pieces | To roll slowly along the grass
exercise: In basketball, what is a rebound? | A shot that goes into the net | *Catching the ball after a missed shot | Passing the ball to a teammate | A player who runs very fast
exercise: «Prices rebounded in the summer.» What does this suggest? | *Prices went back up after going down | Prices stayed exactly the same | Prices were hidden away
test: «Sam jumped high and got the rebound.» In this sentence, what kind of word is rebound? | A question word | *A noun, a naming word | A verb, a doing word
test: «The ball rebounds off the post each time.» Which word means the same as rebounds here? | *bounces back | sinks | freezes | stays still
exam: «After the missed shot, the player caught the rebound.» What does rebound mean? | To fall asleep | *The ball caught after a missed shot | A ball that was never thrown | A kind of trainer
